From 4b2375977df873be57bc277b17778f94323ef7e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason McCartney <jmacAJ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:57:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] perf(exl3): group fat-expert prefill on GPU

Replace the host-synchronized per-expert fat path with a device task planner and five phase-wide launches specialized for GLM-5.3 K4 H4096/I1024 TP2. Promote it in the two-Spark launcher with an immediate env rollback.

Provenance:
- https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3 at c5d9c657966ffeeaa9353f0cc899f18629da4a13: K4 trellis decode, Hadamard helpers, and tensor-core MMA foundations used by the existing arithmetic kernel.
- https://github.com/Reederey87/glm53-flash-exl3-2x-dgx-spark at 0c03250cd7176a2fef9cbbf9329fed08c8750e7d: cp.async M64 fat-GEMM pipeline adapted by the existing local kernel and reused here. No grouped-prefill implementation was copied.

Original work:
- GPU-resident M64 task planner, persistent route scratch, phase-wide cross-expert scheduling, FP32 atomic routed accumulation, exact-shape dispatch, rollback wiring, and comparison gates.

Verification:
- scripts/tinyglm-gate.sh static: PASS.
- Native SM121 image compiled independently on both GB10s; overlay GPU self-check passed.
- Model-free production-shape A/B: max_abs=0; +9.5% to +51.9% across tested expert distributions.
- Full 320B TP2, ~33K actual-token prompts, three paired reps: C1 TTFT -8.8% and effective prefill +9.6%; staggered C2 TTFT p50 -6.1%, p95 -6.0%, wall -5.9%, aggregate effective prefill +6.3%; all requests successful and prefix-cache hit rate 0%.
